17334 |  16 |  * CSR format.
17335 |  17 |  *
17336 |  18 |  * This function implements a partitioning strategy based on destination
17337 |  19 |  * vertices.
17338 |  20 |  * 1.  It identifies all unique destination vertices in the graph.
17339 |  21 |  * 2.  It distributes these destination vertices disjointly and as evenly as
17340 |  22 |  * possible among all available partitions (for both big and little kernels).
17341 |  23 |  * 3.  It assigns each edge from the global graph to the partition that is
17342 |  24 |  * responsible for its destination vertex.
17343 |  25 |  * 4.  For each partition, it collects all unique vertices involved (both
17344 |  26 |  * sources and destinations).
17345 |  27 |  * 5.  It performs vertex ID compression for each partition, creating a local ID
17346 |  28 |  * space. Destination vertices are mapped first to ensure they occupy the lower
17347 |  29 |  * ID range.
17348 |  30 |  * 6.  It rewrites the partition's edges using these new local IDs.
17349 |  31 |  * 7.  Finally, it converts the rewritten edges into a local CSR format.
17350 |  32 |  *
17351 |  33 |  * @param graph The input global graph in CSR format.
